WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.203
Yesterday, two key impeachment
witnesses tied President Trump

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:07.406
and Rudy Giuliani directly to
the quid pro quo with Ukraine,

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.809
and today we saw more fallout
from that bombshell.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.779
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:16.582
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:18.551
Yesterday,
we learned damning new facts

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.586
about the President's
direct involvement

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.490
in a scheme to extort Ukraine
to get them to manufacture dirt

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.824
on his political opponents,

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.826
and yet, today,
a few pundits and reporters

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.028
dismissed the first day
of impeachment hearings,

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.797
which included bombshell
new testimony

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.333
tieing Trump directly to the
scheme, calling them "boring."

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.702
One wrote that unlike
the best reality TV shows,

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.737
not to mention
the Trump presidency itself,

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.140
fireworks and explosive moments
were scarce.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.809
And another wrote that the first
two witnesses called Wednesday

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.410
testified to Trump's scheme

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:47.613
but lacked the pizzazz necessary
to capture public attention.

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:49.882
What do you mean
it lacked pizzazz?

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:52.085
The only politicians
who have ever been entertaining

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.953
were the ones in "Hamilton."

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.222
What do you want them to do?
Show up with their own

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.259
backup dancers like
they're in a chorus line?

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.727
Or, better yet, maybe chairman
of the committee Adam Schiff

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:04.063
and the rest of the Democrats
can interpret the hearings

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.632
through the music of "Cats."

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:09.536
"Ambassador, do Jellicles
engage in quid pro quo?"

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.036
"Congressman, all I can say

00:01:11.036 --> 00:01:13.506
is Jellicles can
and Jellicles do."

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.374
But the people
who are especially invested

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:17.876
in writing off the impeachment
hearings as a media spectacle

00:01:17.876 --> 00:01:20.246
were of course Trump's defenders
in the Republican Party

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.715
and on Fox News,
who dismissed the entire thing

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.585
as a fake scandal
invented by Democrats for TV.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.020
-What we will witness today

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.156
is a televised
theatrical performance

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.058
staged by the Democrats.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.660
It seems you agreed,
witting or unwittingly,

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.929
to participate in a drama.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:40.032
-Well, the Democrats' TV show
on impeachment

00:01:40.032 --> 00:01:41.400
starts tomorrow morning.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.636
-We read the transcript
from behind closed doors.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.037
It's almost like
the pregame show.

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:46.539
Then all these people
fall into place

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:49.341
as if it was a Hollywood script.
-This is a television show.

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:52.144
It's all about trying to create

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:55.347
some kind of environment
and to create a spectacle.

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:58.117
Adam Schiff loves
television cameras.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:01.420
I've never seen anyone
who would risk his life

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.489
to jump in front of one
like he does.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.491
-You think Schiff
would risk his life

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.026
to jump in front of a camera?

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.495
Donald Trump is always on TV.

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:12.832
If Trump saw a camera
on the other side of a canyon,

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:17.570
he'd strap himself to a rocket
like Wile E. Coyote.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.704
Now, you might remember

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:20.339
that before
the public hearings started,

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:22.074
Republicans complained
about the rules,

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:23.976
claiming that because Democrats
were holding

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.511
private, closed-door
depositions,

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:27.446
the process
was somehow illegitimate.

00:02:27.446 --> 00:02:29.682
Well, Republicans got
their wish, and Democrats

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.218
held their first public
impeachment hearing yesterday,

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.987
and then Republicans
were completely satisfied

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.122
and they accepted the process
and never complained again.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:39.458
-Well, they shouldn't be
having public hearings.

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:40.760
This is a hoax.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.795
-So now you don't want
public hearings, either?!

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.030
Then what do you want? 'Cause
it's either public or private.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.467
You gotta pick one. You can't
treat impeachment hearings

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.402
like a rookie cop
defusing a bomb.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.471
"Cut the red wire?
No, the blue wire.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.339
No, it's the red wire.
Wait! I got an idea!

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.174
Rudy, come sit on this bomb!"

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:57.209
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.209 --> 00:03:01.147
But now -- now we very much
are having public hearings,

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.449
and we learned something damning

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.050
from the first hearing
yesterday.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.253
One of the witnesses,
Ambassador Bill Taylor,

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.388
revealed that a staffer
had overheard Trump

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:12.025
talking on the phone
with one of his key henchmen,

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.493
a guy named Gordon Sondland,

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.494
about the quid pro quo
with Ukraine.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:18.631
-Taylor said a staffer of his
recently told him

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:21.934
about this conversation
involving the President

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:25.104
and the Trump donor
turned ambassador to the EU,

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.538
Gordon Sondland.

00:03:26.538 --> 00:03:28.808
-In the presence of my staff
at a restaurant,

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.344
Ambassador Sondland
called President Trump

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:34.046
and told him
of his meetings in Kiev.

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:35.381
The member of my staff

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.750
could hear President Trump
on the phone

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.820
asking Ambassador Sondland
about the investigations.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.087
-This was a cellphone,
I take it?

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:43.389
-It was a cellphone.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.291
-The President must have been
speaking loud enough

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.060
for your staff member
to be able to overhear this?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.563
-He was.
-That's right.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:52.598
Trump was so loud,
people overheard him

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:54.033
on the other end of the call.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.935
I'm shocked he didn't
just go all the way

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.404
and take the call
while he was on national TV.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.939
"There was nothing illegal.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.440
Oh, hold on. Let me take this.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.376
Oh, good. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
The extortion? Great.

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:05.344
And the bribery?
That's fantastic.

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:08.147
Should we -- Should we throw
another crime in there?

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.750
Maybe, like, fraud?
All right. Fantastic.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.785
All right.
Gotta go. Press conference."

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:16.222
And then, today, the AP reported
that a second U.S. official

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.957
had also heard Trump's call
with Sondland,

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.359
and yet when Trump was asked
yesterday about that phone call,

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:22.027
he pretended he didn't know
anything about it.

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:25.297
-There was one moment
where Ambassador Bill Taylor

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:29.201
recounted a conversation
that an aide of his overheard

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:32.070
in which the aide says that he
overheard you say to Sondland,

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.307
"How are things going

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.542
with the proceeding
with the investigations?"

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.011
Is that correct?
And can you fill in some more --

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:41.414
-I know nothing about that.
First time I've heard it.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:43.516
-Do you recall having
a conversation with...

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:45.651
-I don't recall, no, not at all.
Not even a little bit.

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.287
-Oh, not even a little bit.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:51.189
You know Trump is lying when
he goes overboard like that.

00:04:51.189 --> 00:04:54.026
It's like if you asked someone,
"Did you rob that bank?"

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:55.561
Most people would say,
"Of course not."

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.431
Trump would say, "I've never
even been inside a bank.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:00.700
I keep all my money
stuffed inside my coat.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.003
That's why it always
looks like that.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:07.206
It's my fortune. Packed in."

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:09.341
[ Applause ]

00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:11.911
And yet even as Republicans
pretended to complain about

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.413
the supposed media spectacle
of impeachment hearings,

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:16.448
they were looking to get in
on the act themselves.

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:18.984
In fact, this week,
CNN reported that Rudy Giuliani

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:21.520
is considering re-entering
the impeachment fray

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.356
by launching a podcast
to provide impeachment analysis

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:26.426
of the public hearings
in the House of Representatives.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:28.194
Okay, first of all,
you can't do a podcast on

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:31.130
impeachment hearings when you're
a key figure in those hearings.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.465
That would be like a murderer

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.934
hosting an episode
of "Dateline."

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:38.771
"Tonight, I try to track down
my wife's killer,

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.207
and I try to get away."

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:44.210
♪♪

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.245
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.147
Also, you can't do
a crime podcast

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:51.183
about an open-and-shut case.
There's nothing to investigate.

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:52.451
This whole thing would make for

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:54.586
the shortest episode
of "Serial" in history.

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:56.255
-"Hello. I'm Sarah Koenig.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.991
On this episode,
my guest is Rudy Giuliani.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.726
Rudy, did you do it?"

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:04.063
-Of course, I did!

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.398
-"This has been 'Serial.'"

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:08.935
Although, personally,
I have to say the weirdest thing

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:10.736
about this Rudy podcast story
for us

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:13.606
is that we accidentally
predicted it a few months ago

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.741
when we first covered
Rudy's attempts

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:18.276
to dig up dirt on Joe Biden
back in May.

00:06:18.276 --> 00:06:20.579
The best thing about Rudy
is he just admits everything.

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.748
We probably wouldn't have needed
the Mueller Report

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:26.252
if we had just given Rudy
a podcast.

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:29.488
Oh, my God.
We're in Rudy's head, you guys!

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:31.457
It's like in a movie
when the FBI agent

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.359
has to start thinking
like the killer.

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:34.961
In fact,
to predict Rudy's next move,

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.762
I've been doing
the same things he does --

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:39.966
smoking cigars, reading my iPad,
and sitting on my own balls.

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:42.568
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:45.037
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.806
You know, I bet Rudy doing a
podcast would really help Trump

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:50.276
because if there's one thing
you can say about Rudy,

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:52.545
it's that he always makes
a convincing argument.

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:55.080
-We got an anonymous
whistleblower who says

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.982
that Donald Trump
did something wrong.

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:59.285
Donald Trump,
like Hunter Biden says,

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:00.653
I didn't do anything wrong.

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:03.189
This all should have stopped
when President Trump said,

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:04.756
"I didn't do anything wrong."

00:07:04.756 --> 00:07:06.658
-Oh, is that
when it should have stopped?

00:07:06.658 --> 00:07:08.193
When Trump said so?

00:07:08.193 --> 00:07:10.095
That argument only works
with 5-year-olds.

00:07:10.095 --> 00:07:11.397
"Clean your room."
"Why?"

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:14.834
"Because I said so."
"Damn it! You got me!"

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:16.435
Seriously,
is that your argument?

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:17.736
I have a hard time believing

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:19.905
Rudy has ever actually
tried a case in a courtroom.

00:07:19.905 --> 00:07:21.640
"Your Honor, my client says
he didn't do it,

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.075
so I think we can all
go home now.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:25.077
And on your way home,
check out my new podcast,

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.679
"My Client Did It,
and Here's How."

00:07:27.679 --> 00:07:29.681
So the first day
of the impeachment hearings

00:07:29.681 --> 00:07:31.250
directly tied
both Trump and Rudy

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.452
to the Ukraine scheme,
which underscores yet again

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:35.687
that Rudy is a central figure
in this whole thing.

00:07:35.687 --> 00:07:38.190
In fact, two of his associates
who helped him dig up dirt

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.725
in Ukraine
have already been arrested.

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:41.661
Remember those two guys?
Lev and Igor?

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:43.295
Those are their real names,

00:07:43.295 --> 00:07:46.198
although it's impossible to keep
track of which one is which.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:47.967
They look like
they played the burglars

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:51.170
in the Ukrainian remake
of "Home Alone."

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:55.140
But we found out this week
that Trump had at least

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.109
ten separate interactions
with these guys,

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:59.578
which means Trump was lying
when he said he had no idea

00:07:59.578 --> 00:08:02.314
who they were when they were
first arrested last month.

00:08:02.314 --> 00:08:04.150
-Sir, what conversations
have you had

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.085
with Lev Parnas and Igor Fruman?

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.987
-I don't know those gentlemen.

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:10.389
-Oh, you don't know
those gentlemen?

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:12.658
Whenever an idiot like Trump
suddenly reverts

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:15.026
to 18th-century diction,
you know he's nervous.

00:08:15.026 --> 00:08:17.996
It's as if your wife
confronted you about an affair,

00:08:17.996 --> 00:08:19.898
and you were like,
"Janice? Why, I, uh, have never

00:08:19.898 --> 00:08:24.736
had a pleasure of making
that gentlelady's acquaintance.

00:08:24.736 --> 00:08:27.205
Despite what you might hear
from some in the media,

00:08:27.205 --> 00:08:29.775
yesterday's impeachment hearing
provided damning new evidence,

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.577
making clear that Trump and Rudy

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.779
were both directly involved
in the Ukraine scheme.

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.447
Everyone should watch
these hearings

00:08:35.447 --> 00:08:37.082
because they make clear
without a doubt

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:39.185
that Trump and Rudy
are not innocent.

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:40.719
-Not even a little bit.

00:08:40.719 --> 00:08:42.554
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:08:42.554 --> 00:08:44.891
♪♪

